      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1438457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-29T12:55:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The thing is that is we use start the test run with a console command e.g. `ztest run-all` it is done only once by a test runner. The `abort` call causes reboot and after reboot the test is not running anymore, so we need to trigger the run one more time based on the test state.",
